WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:03.900
Hi everybody! I’m Tom from BBC Learning English.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.340
People often confuse the words

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.860
specially and especially.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.590
Today, I'm going to tell you the difference.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:16.180
Both of these words are adverbs.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.920
Especially means 'in particular' or 'most of all'.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.260
For example:

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.080
I like food,

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.260
but I especially like sandwiches.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.160
This means that I particularly like sandwiches.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.740
They're my favourite kind of food.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.660
Specially, however, has a different meaning.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.300
Specially means

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.140
'for a particular purpose' or 'in a particular way'.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.120
So:

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.160
This sandwich was specially made.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:57.300
Dan made a special sandwich just for me.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.340
Thank you, Dan!

